From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:00:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The wind comes in gusts, each from its own way

Patch 0047 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08: "it doesn't seem like the varied direction is like changing ... it needs to
like have ramp-ups that you know the gust happens in one direction and then it kind of slows down
and particles just kind of float around. And then another gust happens but it goes in a completely
different direction and then it slows down. It needs to act very natural", modeled on a reference
of theirs; then "fully 3D, as in you know, 360 around, but as far as up and down ... limit the
cone", and "it can also gust down and then up or up and then down".

0036 and 0041 moved the dust by a closed form of the time; 0041's varied wind turned on waves of 75
and 200 seconds, so in play its direction never visibly changed. The wind is now stepped on the CPU
with a real clock (stepWind, called each trace): a base breeze that swells and eases and, for the
varied wind, meanders in heading; and gusts one at a time, each with its own heading (anywhere for
the varied wind, within 40 degrees of the base for a set one), its own tilt between 12 degrees
below level and 18 above, wavering by up to 8 degrees inside that while it blows, and its own
strength (two to five times the base, weaker for Light gusts), that ramp up, hold with a flutter
and fade, with a calm of a few seconds between (longer for Light). The air follows that wind with
drag, so it keeps moving after a gust and slows instead of stopping. The shader takes how far the
air has carried the dust (tuneWindField.xyz) in place of windOffset, which is gone.

diff --git a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
--- a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 #include "rt64_framebuffer_renderer.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cmath>
 #include <cstring>
 
 #include "../include/rt64_extended_gbi.h"
@@ -1291,6 +1293,148 @@ namespace RT64 {
     }
 
 #if RT_ENABLED
+    // THE WIND, GUST BY GUST (patch 0047, the user, 2026-10-08: "it doesn't seem like the varied
+    // direction is like changing ... it needs to like have ramp-ups that you know the gust happens in
+    // one direction and then it kind of slows down and particles just kind of float around. And
+    // then another gust happens but it goes in a completely different direction and then it slows
+    // down. It needs to act very natural"; and a reference of theirs whose wind they want this to
+    // behave like). 0036 and 0041 moved the dust by a closed form of the time, and 0041's varied
+    // wind turned on waves of 75 and 200 seconds, so in play its direction never visibly changed.
+    //
+    // This is the reference's model, on the CPU with a real clock: a gentle base breeze whose
+    // strength swells and eases and, for the varied wind, whose heading meanders; and gusts, one at
+    // a time, each from its own direction (any for the varied wind, within 40 degrees of the base
+    // for a set one) and of its own strength, that ramp up, hold with a flutter, fade away, and
+    // leave a calm of a few seconds before the next. The AIR follows that wind with drag, so it
+    // keeps moving after a gust and slows down rather than stopping dead, and what the shader
+    // receives is how far the air has carried the dust so far (tuneWindField.xyz) and how fast it
+    // is moving now (w). The rows: the wind's speed is the base breeze in world units a second, a
+    // gust peaks at two to five times it, Light gusts are weaker and rarer than Strong, and None
+    // leaves the base breeze alone.
+    struct WindModel {
+        enum class Gust { Calm, Ramp, Hold, Fade };
+        Gust state = Gust::Calm;
+        float timer = 2.0f;
+        float stateTime = 0.0f;
+        float rampTime = 1.0f;
+        float holdTime = 1.0f;
+        float fadeTime = 2.0f;
+        float peak = 0.0f;
+        float gustHeading = 0.0f;
+        float gustTilt = 0.0f;
+        float gustWaverPhase = 0.0f;
+        float baseHeading = 0.0f;
+        float clock = 0.0f;
+        hlslpp::float3 air = hlslpp::float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+        hlslpp::float3 carried = hlslpp::float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+        uint32_t seed = 0x9E3779B9u;
+        bool started = false;
+        std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point last;
+
+        float random(float low, float high) {
+            seed = seed * 1664525u + 1013904223u;
+            return low + (high - low) * (float(seed >> 8) / 16777216.0f);
+        }
+    };
+
+    static const float WindAirDrag = 1.9f;          // a second's share by which the air closes on the wind (the reference's drag)
+    static const float WindMaxStep = 0.05f;         // seconds at most one step integrates, so a stall never fires a huge jump
+    // A GUST'S TILT IS HELD NEAR LEVEL (the user, 2026-10-08: "gusts wouldn't come directly up from
+    // the ground, so they need to be fully 3D, as in you know, 360 around, but as far as up and down
+    // ... limit the cone"; and "it can also gust down and then up or up and then down"). Its heading
+    // is anywhere round the compass, its tilt between these two, and while it blows the tilt wavers
+    // by up to WindGustWaver either way, still inside them.
+    static const float WindGustDown = 12.0f * 0.0174533f;   // radians below level at most
+    static const float WindGustUp = 18.0f * 0.0174533f;     // radians above level at most
+    static const float WindGustWaver = 8.0f * 0.0174533f;
+
+    static hlslpp::float4 stepWind(const hlslpp::float4 &tuneWind) {
+        static WindModel wind;
+        const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        float dt = 0.0f;
+        if (wind.started) {
+            dt = std::min(std::chrono::duration<float>(now - wind.last).count(), WindMaxStep);
+        }
+        else {
+            wind.started = true;
+            wind.baseHeading = wind.random(0.0f, 6.2831853f);
+        }
+
+        wind.last = now;
+        wind.clock += dt;
+
+        const float speed = std::max(float(tuneWind.z), 0.0f);
+        const float gusts = std::clamp(float(tuneWind.w), 0.0f, 1.0f);
+        const bool varied = (float(tuneWind.x) == 0.0f) && (float(tuneWind.y) == 0.0f);
+        const float setHeading = std::atan2(float(tuneWind.y), float(tuneWind.x));
+        if (varied) {
+            wind.baseHeading += std::sin(wind.clock * 0.07f) * dt * 0.25f;
+        }
+
+        const float heading = varied ? wind.baseHeading : setHeading;
+        const float baseStrength = speed * (1.0f + 0.35f * std::sin(wind.clock * 0.23f));
+        hlslpp::float3 target = hlslpp::float3(std::cos(heading), 0.0f, std::sin(heading)) * baseStrength;
+
+        if ((gusts > 0.0f) && (speed > 0.0f)) {
+            switch (wind.state) {
+            case WindModel::Gust::Calm:
+                wind.timer -= dt;
+                if (wind.timer <= 0.0f) {
+                    wind.gustHeading = varied ? wind.random(0.0f, 6.2831853f) : (setHeading + wind.random(-0.7f, 0.7f));
+                    wind.gustTilt = wind.random(-WindGustDown, WindGustUp);
+                    wind.gustWaverPhase = wind.random(0.0f, 6.2831853f);
+                    wind.peak = speed * wind.random(2.0f, 5.0f) * (0.4f + 0.6f * gusts);
+                    wind.rampTime = wind.random(0.4f, 1.2f);
+                    wind.holdTime = wind.random(0.3f, 1.6f);
+                    wind.fadeTime = wind.random(1.8f, 4.2f);
+                    wind.state = WindModel::Gust::Ramp;
+                    wind.stateTime = 0.0f;
+                }
+                break;
+            default:
+                wind.stateTime += dt;
+                break;
+            }
+
+            float force = 0.0f;
+            if (wind.state == WindModel::Gust::Ramp) {
+                const float t = std::min(1.0f, wind.stateTime / wind.rampTime);
+                force = wind.peak * t * t;
+                if (wind.stateTime >= wind.rampTime) {
+                    wind.state = WindModel::Gust::Hold;
+                    wind.stateTime = 0.0f;
+                }
+            }
+            else if (wind.state == WindModel::Gust::Hold) {
+                force = wind.peak * (0.92f + 0.08f * std::sin(wind.clock * 9.0f));
+                if (wind.stateTime >= wind.holdTime) {
+                    wind.state = WindModel::Gust::Fade;
+                    wind.stateTime = 0.0f;
+                }
+            }
+            else if (wind.state == WindModel::Gust::Fade) {
+                const float t = std::min(1.0f, wind.stateTime / wind.fadeTime);
+                force = wind.peak * (1.0f - (1.0f - (1.0f - t) * (1.0f - t)));
+                if (wind.stateTime >= wind.fadeTime) {
+                    wind.state = WindModel::Gust::Calm;
+                    // Light gusts come further apart than strong ones.
+                    wind.timer = wind.random(1.6f, 5.5f) * (2.0f - gusts);
+                }
+            }
+
+            const float tilt = std::clamp(wind.gustTilt + WindGustWaver * std::sin(wind.clock * 1.1f + wind.gustWaverPhase), -WindGustDown, WindGustUp);
+            const hlslpp::float3 gustDirection(std::cos(tilt) * std::cos(wind.gustHeading), std::sin(tilt), std::cos(tilt) * std::sin(wind.gustHeading));
+            target += gustDirection * force;
+        }
+        else {
+            wind.state = WindModel::Gust::Calm;
+        }
+
+        wind.air += (target - wind.air) * std::min(1.0f, WindAirDrag * dt);
+        wind.carried += wind.air * dt;
+        return hlslpp::float4(float(wind.carried.x), float(wind.carried.y), float(wind.carried.z), float(hlslpp::length(wind.air)));
+    }
+
